header><div class=3D"Post-body"><p>My favorite way to learn Godot is to fol=
low tutorials that teach you how to build a full game, I've been on the hun=
t for the best ones and I thought I'd document my finds, keep in mind that =
there's many more but these are just the ones that I've found to have the b=
est quality, they'll teach you the how and why of everything, please feel f=
ree to Mention other cool tutorials I've missed</p>

<h3><strong>-------Godot 3 tutorials-------</strong></h3>

<p><a href=3D"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3DWEt2JHEe-do&amp;t=3D10s" re=
l=3D"ugc nofollow">your First 2D game "Dodge the creeps" by GDquest</a> (te=
aches the very basics)</p>

<p><a href=3D"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3DYiE9tcoCfhE" rel=3D"ugc nof=
ollow">your first 3D game "Squash the creeps" by GDquest</a> (also teaches =
the very basics but 3D !)</p>

<p><a href=3D"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3Dkr1BoEbuveI&amp;t=3D6937s" =
rel=3D"ugc nofollow">Learn Godot by creating Pong, by Clear Code</a> (very =
well edited and explains everything greatly)</p>

<p><a href=3D"https://youtube.com/playlist?list=3DPLhXFaKLHQJdVbOCcP7OBOUnc=
tsZRkl3KJ&amp;si=3DSbhLDyt9cjRHBHUb" rel=3D"ugc nofollow">Create Flappy Bir=
d In Godot 3 by kaan alpar</a> (simple to follow and creates a very polishe=
d game)</p>

<p><a href=3D"https://youtube.com/playlist?list=3DPLbxeTux6kwSDl_IuXDCnWdS_=
dQlqDzgV5&amp;si=3Dwgkwz14h1FrfuhVI" rel=3D"ugc nofollow">Asteroids in Godo=
t 3.4 by SRCoder</a> (this tutorial is great but there's a bug that never g=
ets fixed, I managed to easily fix it on my own though)</p>

<p><a href=3D"https://youtube.com/playlist?list=3DPLah6faXAgguPlyHWM5G9in10=
UzRcdeb2R&amp;si=3DD4UUtPbqG3gv5vKN" rel=3D"ugc nofollow">Yet another space=
 shooter by CodeNMore</a> (amazing and teaches you how to implement a ton o=
f cool things like classes for the enemies and CPU particles)</p>

<p><a href=3D"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3D-I_AdBkryoU" rel=3D"ugc nof=
ollow">Creating Snake in Godot by ClearCode</a> (haven't watched it yet but=
 it's by the same creator who made the Pong tutorial so it should be great)=
</p>

<p><a href=3D"https://youtube.com/playlist?list=3DPLhqJJNjsQ7KH_z21S_XeXD3H=
t3WnSqW97&amp;si=3DveXQbxu12KYfy6d2" rel=3D"ugc nofollow">Make Your First 2=
D Platformer Game with Godot by GDquest</a> (another great GDquest course)<=
/p>

<p><a href=3D"https://youtube.com/playlist?list=3DPL9FzW-m48fn2SlrW0KoLT4n5=
egNdX-W9a&amp;si=3DD2uv45iORY6DD-IU" rel=3D"ugc nofollow">Godot action RPG =
series by HeartBeast</a> (haven't seen this one but HeartBeast makes qualit=
y tutorials !)</p>

<p><a href=3D"https://youtube.com/playlist?list=3DPL9FzW-m48fn1JgK_mavg7ym6=
nvchF9Yjb&amp;si=3D-utB9hqFlSOn3st4" rel=3D"ugc nofollow">Godot Mobile Turn=
 based RPG by HeartBeast</a> (another HeartBeast series)</p>

<p><a href=3D"https://youtube.com/playlist?list=3DPL6bQeQE-ybqAYoaWz_ZEE2X4=
wX6PhwCWR&amp;si=3Da6ZCi4KewEHE1KrT" rel=3D"ugc nofollow">Godot Wave Shoote=
r Tutorials by PlugWorld </a> (I didn't watch this one but the fianl game l=
ooks amazing)</p>

<p><a href=3D"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3DHmnwNadwHWI&amp;t=3D55s" re=
l=3D"ugc nofollow"> Make your first 2D grid-based game from scratch </a> (h=
aven't seen it yet but it looks pretty good)</p>

<h3><strong>-------Godot 4 tutorials-------</strong></h3>

<p><a href=3D"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3DGwCiGixlqiU&amp;t=3D6694s" =
rel=3D"ugc nofollow">Your First 2D GAME From Zero with GODOT 4! <strong>Vam=
pire Survivor Style</strong> by GDquest </a> (probably my favorite tutorial=
 ever)</p>

<p><a href=3D"https://youtube.com/playlist?list=3DPL9FzW-m48fn0i9GYBoTY-SI3=
yOBZjH1kJ&amp;si=3D5S1cwGfW99lb17S-" rel=3D"ugc nofollow">Heart Platformer =
- Godot 4 Tutorial Series by HeartBeast</a> (I've only just started it but =
it looks pretty solid)</p>

<p><a href=3D"https://youtube.com/playlist?list=3DPLMQtM2GgbPEVuTgD4Ln17omb=
Tg6EahSLr&amp;si=3DcicTqYfpFaHjJRKS" rel=3D"ugc nofollow">Action RPG in God=
ot 4 tutorial series by Maker Tech </a> (I've only seen parts of it but fro=
m what I've seen it's very well done and explains everything very clearly a=
nd creates a polished game)</p>

<p><a href=3D"https://youtube.com/playlist?list=3DPL3cGrGHvkwn3Zi2BRFgdemV6=
T6afvWTFx&amp;si=3DKHH4G1HjKMAZgmgc" rel=3D"ugc nofollow">Godot Hack'n'Slas=
h Course by DevWorm</a> (only seen a bit of it but the game created has a l=
ot of cool features + the creator is a pretty cool guy )</p>

<p><a href=3D"https://youtube.com/playlist?list=3DPLMb6Yv6-w-RWngEjn_YeMzVw=
gyXBZ73Bf&amp;si=3DdWNYkXWAo155WGUw" rel=3D"ugc nofollow"> Godot 4 Platform=
er  by GameDevKnight</a> (only watched a bit of it but it looks pretty nice=
)</p>

<p><a href=3D"https://youtube.com/playlist?list=3DPL6SABXRSlpH8CD71L7zye311=
cp9R4JazJ&amp;si=3DZEN0sr9yRICdAH-A" rel=3D"ugc nofollow">Godot 4 Intermedi=
ate Card Game Course by GodotGameLab</a> (this is a more advanced and lengt=
hy 2 season series, so you should probably have some experience before foll=
owing it)</p>

<p><a href=3D"https://youtube.com/playlist?list=3DPLGZeG39sIjYs-eKQhSBK4_nh=
4ONasjMLw&amp;si=3DHbtoHL2LJ-Va6gpd" rel=3D"ugc nofollow">2D Metroidvania G=
odot 4.2 by Jean Makes Games</a> (this series isn't fully complete but it t=
eaches you how to make the player movement abilities and combat + a working=
 tile-map, I followed it myself and just used my own knowledge to create an=
 enemy along with other things that were missing, overall it's pretty great=
 if you wanna create a hollow knight clone like me haha)</p>

<p><a href=3D"https://youtube.com/playlist?list=3DPL2-ArCpIQtjELkyLKec8BaVV=
CeunuHSK9&amp;si=3DF7eeoHOiBQNqqTTT" rel=3D"ugc nofollow"> Make a Godot Rog=
uelike by Matinator</a> (this course has no voice over for the first 75% of=
 it and it needs some experience to be followed as it covers things like pr=
ocedural generation , but the end result should be pretty awesome, there's =
even a demo you can play of the final game you're gonna create)</p>

<p><a href=3D"https://youtube.com/playlist?list=3DPLuQJapu7L84Qm0libslNu4CN=
6yILH8QIL&amp;si=3Do_P8XatN16nkPOFE" rel=3D"ugc nofollow"> Godot 4 - Roguel=
ike by Marcial Lincoln</a> (this course is in Spanish, I myself don't speak=
 that but I thought I'd include it here anyway as other people could benefi=
t from it, you're gonna create a grid based Rogue-like similar to the origi=
nal Rogue, which looks neat)</p>

<p><a href=3D"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3DFNEAJsry5sA" rel=3D"ugc nof=
ollow">Complete 2D Platformer in Godot 4 Tutorial - Zero to Shipped Game fo=
r Beginners by Brett Makes Games</a> (I haven't seen it but it's shorter th=
an the other platformer tutorials that I included)</p>

<p><a href=3D"https://youtube.com/playlist?list=3DPLtosjGHWDab682nfZ1f6JSQ1=
cjap7Ieeb&amp;si=3Dpf3CAKmFqz1cUuKM" rel=3D"ugc nofollow">Make a Vampire Su=
rvivors Clone in Godot 4 by Branno</a> (a more advanced and lengthy course =
to remake the iconic Vampire Survivors)</p>

<p><a href=3D"https://youtube.com/playlist?list=3DPL3cGrGHvkwn2NOT1LSwf5d2X=
Zmlc5Bjsn&amp;si=3D2O88PDTNqzOVDasA" rel=3D"ugc nofollow">How to Make a Sur=
vival Game in Godot by DevWorm</a> (another DevWorm course, teaches you coo=
l things like making an inventory system and NPCs and even cut-scenes)</p><=
